Z||000000||Bluebottlejunky||08-12-2001||02:14 AM||||ok, well i got my top part of my engine back togeather from painting..(plenum, middle plenum, fuel rail, valve covers)..all hooked up..anyway..got it started and everything..set timing better so at idle is is bit louder than befor and idles at about 1000-900rpm. anyway..went for a drive..but when i drive..like say put the gas down it dosent wanna go..it kinda dose just not very fast..kinda hesitates..at times it will go..like fast then slow...im not getting any new codes. Any ideas please?  Could timing still be off?..Something ignition wise?  Maybe something on the TB (sensors cables etc) any help or leads will help thanks!<P>------------------<BR>Hello, My name is Mike and I am addicted too fiero's...PLEASE dont help me.<BR>85'GT 4sp<BR>AIM: Fierofanatic2001||||reg||1
Z||000001||maryjane||08-12-2001||03:34 AM||||did you have the battery disconnected while doing the work? Maybe you didn't drive it far enough for the ECM to reset itself. My idle did the same thing and car ran like it was pulling an 18 wheeler. Mine took about 15 miles and didn't run right until I had coaxed it up to 55, then it took off, been fine ever since.<p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 08-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Songman||08-12-2001||05:03 AM||||Possible vacuum leak somewhere?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||08-12-2001||05:24 AM||||Could be a vacuum leak like Somgman says or you could have a bad sensor. Check the connectors on your sensors and the vacuum ports on the TB for missing hoses.<BR>Also, the IAC sensor requires that you drive at or over 40mph for at least 10 seconds to reset it.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 08-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||artherd||08-12-2001||05:30 AM||||uh, you timed by sound?  try a timing light at 10degree BTDC, and remember to do this after shorting the ECU to open-loop mode.<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
